# The plan ground of the map — `docs/adr/0005-map-and-tile-path.md` §2 and §3, and #73.
#
# Leave it empty and the map draws the plan ground from the servers of the OpenStreetMap
# Foundation. That fallback is what makes the application run with no configuration at all, and
# **#73 holds what must be true before any deployment**: that policy is for casual and low-volume
# use, and it is not a tile service for an application.
#
# Set it to the tile template of a hosted archive, and the map uses that instead. The template
# takes `{z}`, `{x}` and `{y}`.
#
#   VITE_MAP_PLAN_TILES=https://tiles.example.invalid/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local`, which git ignores.
VITE_MAP_PLAN_TILES=

# The PostgREST read API. It serves the `api` schema on the loopback address only.
#
# Leave it empty and the application reads from `http://127.0.0.1:3000`, which is the address the
# local compose file publishes. That fallback is the second half of what makes the application run
# with no configuration at all. Set it to the address of another read service, and the application
# reads from that instead. A value that is set but malformed stops the read.
VITE_API_URL=
